    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Observe that \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3+\\sqrt5)\\\\ &\\quad{}\\cdot(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3-\\sqrt5)\\\\ &=(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3)^2-5\\\\ &=2\\sqrt6. \\end{aligned} \\] Hence the quotient is \\(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3-\\sqrt5.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Group the first two radicals in the denominator",
        "Multiply \\(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3+\\sqrt5\\) by \\(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3-\\sqrt5\\)"
      ],
